<p>Hi <%= @first_name %>,</p>

<p>
  The Airtable sync for <strong><%= @event.name %></strong> has failed
  <strong><%= pluralize(@failures, "time") %> in a row</strong>. Attend is still retrying
  every 5 minutes, because errors like this are usually Airtable rate limiting the base
  or having an outage, which clear up by themselves. If the error below looks like
  something else, the settings may need fixing.
</p>

<p>You're getting this because you were the last person to save the Airtable settings for this event.</p>

<div style="border: 1px solid #f5c2c7; background-color: #fdf2f3; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <p style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;"><strong>What Airtable said:</strong></p>
  <p style="margin: 0; font-family: monospace; font-size: 13px; word-break: break-all;"><%= @error_message %></p>
</div>

<p>
  If it doesn't recover, check that nothing else is sending a lot of requests to the
  same base, and look at <a href="https://status.airtable.com">status.airtable.com</a>.
</p>

<p><%= mail_button "View Airtable sync", @integrations_url %></p>

<p style="color: #6b7280; font-size: 13px;">
  <% if @last_synced_at %>
    Last successful sync was <%= @last_synced_at.strftime("%b %-d, %Y at %-I:%M %p %Z") %> —
    Airtable still shows that data.
  <% else %>
    This integration has never synced successfully.
  <% end %>
  We'll only email again if it fails for a while after its next successful sync.
</p>

<p>If you're not the right person for this any more, just reply and we'll sort it out.</p>
